Alright, the user asked to improve the logo animation. I've already made a few tweaks: adjusted the fill animation timing and easing, added a stroke-out animation to the draw segment, and refined the draw segment timing syntax. Those changes should make the animation smoother and give a nicer fade-out effect after the sweep.

Now I need to consider what else might be lacking. Looking at the current CSS snippets I've edited, I see that the sweep animation (`aiLogoSweep202606`) has a hardcoded delay of `1.55s`. If the user wants to tweak the timing later, they'd have to edit the CSS directly. It would be better to expose that delay as a CSS variable, similar to how other timings are parameterized (`--duration`, `--fill-delay`, etc.). That way, the user can easily adjust the sweep delay via an inline style or a data attribute without digging into the stylesheet.

Also, I haven't yet accounted for users who prefer reduced motion. The page currently doesn't have any media query to disable animations for those users. Adding a `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` block would be a nice accessibility improvement: we can turn off all animations, ensure the SVG appears static, and make the fill source visible. This aligns with modern best practices.

Finally, I should define the keyframes for the new stroke-out animation (`aiLogoStrokeOut202606`) that I referenced earlier in the draw segment edit. Right now, the keyframes aren't present, so the animation would do nothing. I need to add a simple keyframe that animates opacity to 0.

Putting this together, the edit should:
1. Replace the hardcoded sweep delay with a variable `var(--sweep-delay,1.55s)`.
2. Append the `@keyframes aiLogoStrokeOut202606` definition that fades opacity to 0.
3. Add a `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` block that disables all animations on the logo and ensures the fill source is visible.

I need to locate the exact block in `logo.html` that contains the sweep animation and the existing keyframes. Scanning the file, I find this segment:

```
      transform:translateX(-90%) skewX(-16deg);
      animation:aiLogoSweep202606 .65s ease 1.55s both;
    }
    @keyframes aiLogoDrawSegment202606{to{stroke-dasharray:var(--segment-length) var(--path-length);}}
    @keyframes aiLogoFillIn202606{to{opacity:1;}}
```

This is the exact `old_string` I need to replace. The new string will incorporate the variable delay, add the new keyframes, and include the reduced-motion media query with the appropriate overrides.

Thus, I'll issue an Edit tool call on `/home/lane/log/logo.html`, replacing that old block with the new, expanded block. This should complete the improvements and give the user more flexibility and accessibility.

Now, execute the edit.

